<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/5th-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Plataea</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/479-bce">479 BCE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century-bce">5th century BCE</a> · Also known as Plataea · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greco-persian-wars">Greco-Persian Wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Plataea was fought in 479 BCE in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boeotia">Boeotia</a>, where an allied Greek army led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sparta">Sparta</a> defeated the Persian land forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mardonius">Mardonius</a>. It ended the second Persian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-persian-invasion-of-greece">invasion of Greece</a>. The defeat marked the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaemenid-empire">Achaemenid Empire</a>'s attempts to conquer mainland <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-plataea.jpg" alt="Battle of Plataea" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: John Steeple Davis · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Scene_of_the_Battle_of_Plataea.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
